From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: number the bridges on family D
 too

"make L2/LUT access work on family D" stops advertising fdb_isolation
and max_num_bridges on family D, which has no EFID. Without
max_num_bridges the DSA core gives every bridge number 0, and under the
rtl8365mb-8021q tagger a bridge's number picks its tag_8021q VID:
dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(0) is 3072, the standalone VID of port 0. On
the IPQ5018 boards that port is wan, so every bridge would share its
VLAN with wan, and two bridges would share one with each other.

Keep fdb_isolation off on family D, as that series wants, but keep
max_num_bridges so that the bridges are numbered. Nothing on family D
uses the number for the FDB: port_set_efid() is a no-op there.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -4758,13 +4758,15 @@ static int rtl8365mb_setup(struct dsa_sw
 		goto out_teardown_irq;
 
 	ds->assisted_learning_on_cpu_port = true;
-	if (rtl8365mb_get_family(priv) != RTL8365MB_FAMILY_D) {
+	if (rtl8365mb_get_family(priv) != RTL8365MB_FAMILY_D)
 		ds->fdb_isolation = true;
-		/* The EFID is 3 bits, but EFID 0 is reserved for standalone ports.
-		 * The same 7 is what tag_8021q can enumerate (DSA_TAG_8021Q_MAX_NUM_BRIDGES).
-		 */
-		ds->max_num_bridges = FIELD_MAX(RTL8365MB_EFID_MASK);
-	}
+	/* The EFID is 3 bits, but EFID 0 is reserved for standalone ports.
+	 * The same 7 is what tag_8021q can enumerate (DSA_TAG_8021Q_MAX_NUM_BRIDGES).
+	 * Family D has no EFID, but the bridges still need their numbers:
+	 * under the 8021q tagger a bridge's number picks its tag_8021q VID,
+	 * and bridge number 0 gives the VID of standalone port 0.
+	 */
+	ds->max_num_bridges = FIELD_MAX(RTL8365MB_EFID_MASK);
 
 	ds->configure_vlan_while_not_filtering = true;
 
